<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
      Jacob had been away for twenty years.<break time="500ms"/>
      Twenty years in the household of Laban.<break time="500ms"/>
      He had worked, and married, and fathered children.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He had gathered flocks and herds and servants.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But now the time had come to go home.<break time="500ms"/>
      God spoke to Jacob and said, Return to the land of your fathers.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Return to your kindred, and I will be with you.<break time="1800ms"/>

      So Jacob set out with everything he had.<break time="500ms"/>
      His wives Leah and Rachel, his children, his livestock, all he had gained.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The caravan moved slowly across the land.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But ahead of him lay something he had been avoiding for two decades.<break time="500ms"/>
      His brother Esau.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The brother whose birthright he had taken.<break time="500ms"/>
      The brother whose blessing he had stolen.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jacob sent messengers ahead to Esau in the land of Seir.<break time="500ms"/>
      The messengers returned with a single piece of news.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Esau is coming to meet you, and four hundred men are with him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jacob was greatly afraid and distressed.<break time="500ms"/>
      The past was not behind him after all.<break time="1000ms"/>
      It was walking toward him across the open plain.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes the road home passes through the thing we fear most.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
